<title>USA: U.S. Nov existing home sales rose 1.8 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Nov existing home sales rose 1.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of existing U.S. homes rose 1.8 percent in November to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 4.04 million units from 3.97 million units in October, the National Association of Realtors said Monday.</p>
<p>The November sales rate was up 1.0 percent from sales of 4.00 million in November last year.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast November sales of 3.97 million units.  </p>
<p>NAR reported the following details of existing home sales in seasonally adjusted annual rates:</p>
<p> -				   Nov    Oct		  Nov95</p>
<p> -   Units Sold (in mlns)   4.04   3.97		  4.00</p>
<p> -				   Nov    Oct		 Nov96/95</p>
<p> - Units Sold, Pct Change    1.8   -1.5		   1.0</p>
<p> -				   Nov    Oct--Rev from    Nov95</p>
<p> -  Median Price (1,000s)  117.4  116.6  116.4	114.3</p>
<p>Note -- Median sales price is the midpoint where half the homes sold for more and half for less.</p>
<p>    -				  Nov    Oct--Rev from    Nov95</p>
<p>  Units Available (in mlns)   2.24   2.31   2.36	 1.81</p>
<p>   Months' Worth of Supply     6.6    7.0    7.1	  5.4</p>
<p>   FHLMC 30-Year Rate (Pct)   7.62   7.92		  7.48</p>
<p>Note -- FHLMC rate is the Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corp's average commitment rate for 30-year fixed-rate mortgages.</p>
<p>Units sold by region, seasonally adjusted, in 1,000s:</p>
<p>    -			November  October		  Nov95</p>
<p>    -	 Northeast    590.0     620.0		  630.0</p>
<p>    -	   Midwest  1,070.0   1,020.0		1,050.0</p>
<p>    -	     South  1,460.0   1,450.0		1,470.0</p>
<p>    -		West    920.0     880.0		  850.0</p>
<p>Median price by region, unadjusted, in 1,000s of dollars:</p>
<p>    -			November  October--Rev from     Nov95</p>
<p>    -	 Northeast    136.0     137.8    137.8     135.2</p>
<p>    -	   Midwest     99.3	98.0     98.0	95.8</p>
<p>    -	     South    102.4     102.4    102.7	99.4</p>
<p>    -		West    151.9     150.3    149.1     148.7</p>
